 "content": "# Continual-ARC observation: preserve clean solid rectangles

Observed on task-315375b1. The input contains many axis-aligned, solid monochrome rectangular patches on a different background color, with isolated/interior pixels in other colors acting as noise/markers. The output removes all noise/markers and all non-rectangle background, while retaining every solid rectangular patch exactly in its original color and dimensions (including patches whose fill equals a color distinct from the dominant background, e.g. color 0 on background 8).

Demo evidence: a 20x22 grid retained the 5x4 color-5 rectangle and two color-8 rectangles (6x4 and 6x3), removing scattered pixels of colors 1,2,6,9 and all remaining background. Test evidence: retained all clean rectangular patches with colors 6,7,0,9 and removed embedded isolated 2/4 markers and other background. Key practical step: identify complete filled rectangles as contiguous patches; output a clean canvas in the background color with only those rectangles copied over. Do not mistake isolated colored pixels, even within a rectangle, for changes to the patch; replace them with the rectangle's fill color. Preserve original row/column locations and sizes."
